{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_vrtx_01Wu8voZGvbW66KPfDBvKqx9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. I wrote **`answers/03-020-architect-an-agent-system-loop-tools-memory-orchestration-sa.md`** — Q20: *Architect an agent system: loop, tools, memory, orchestration, safety.*\n\nKey content:\n\n- **Concept:** Five interlocking subsystems, each containing a specific failure mode the bare loop can't handle\n- **Loop layer:** `max_iterations=15`, `wall_clock_timeout=120s`, `max_tokens_per_step=2048` — all enforced in orchestrator code, never in a prompt; ReAct/JSON structured action format\n- **Tool layer:** JSON schema contracts, pre-call middleware (schema validation + Presidio PII scrub + auth injection), E2B/Docker sandboxing for code tools, idempotency keys on writes, result truncation to cap observation tokens\n- **Memory (4 tiers):** working (sliding window), episodic (Redis TTL), semantic (Pinecone/Qdrant), procedural (system prompt/tool schemas)\n- **Orchestration:** supervisor-specialist multi-agent pattern; LangGraph DAG for known pipelines vs. open ReAct loop for exploration; orchestration vs. choreography tradeoff table\n- **Safety/observability:** LangSmith structured trace per step, LangGraph `interrupt_before` HITL for irreversible actions, Presidio guardrails on inputs and observations, Redis checkpointing for crash recovery, hard cost cap per run\n- **Example:** Multi-agent legal contract reviewer — supervisor + clause extraction + risk assessment + drafting agents, 300 clauses in 4 min, $0.18/contract\n\n19 more answer notes remain in the Next queue for this category."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":402,"cache_read_input_tokens":67999,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":402,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_